    "knowledge_point": "Computing the Cardinality of a Cartesian Product",
    "problem": "What is the cardinality of $M\\times N$ for $M={a,b,c,d,e,f,g}$ and $N={a,b,c,d,e,f}?$",
    "worked_solution": "For any two finite sets $M$ and $N,$ the cardinality of $M\\times N$ is\n\n$$\n|M\\times N|=|M|\\cdot |N|.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|M\\times N| & =|M|\\cdot |N| \\\\  & =7\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =42.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
